From: ITSMEFRTRUST <215584995+ITSMEFRTRUST@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 00:26:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 059/138] power: supply: Add a driver for the Apple SWI battery
 gauge

The iPhone 6 reads its bq27540 gas gauge like iOS's AppleHDQGasGauge:
HDQ over UART5 at 57600 8N2, one UART frame per HDQ bit (0xfe = 1,
0xc0 = 0), the shared wire echoing every frame, a 9600 baud 0x00 frame
as the break. Before each access the SN2400 charger has to hand the
wire over (register 0x1d = 0x04, wait for bit 5; 0 gives it back).

The gauge has the bq27541 command set, so the bq27xxx core does the
rest. The driver only reads; it never writes to the gauge.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 drivers/power/supply/Kconfig             |   9 +
 drivers/power/supply/Makefile            |   1 +
 drivers/power/supply/apple_swi_battery.c | 454 +++++++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 464 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 drivers/power/supply/apple_swi_battery.c

